# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value below.
#
# IMPORTANT: it is baked into the static build at COMPILE time, not read at
# runtime. If you change it you must re-run `npm run build` and redeploy —
# redeploying alone does nothing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Booking/contact form backend — src/pages/api/submit-form.ts, a Vercel
# serverless function (part of this same project, no separate deploy). It
# receives BOTH the booking modal and the FAQ-page contact form, and sends
# every email through Resend from the verified `thedriver.fr` domain:
#
#   - booking  → chauffeur notification (FR) + customer confirmation (EN)
#   - contact  → chauffeur notification (FR)
#
# The route tells the two apart by the `formType` field in the payload. The
# forms POST to it same-origin (`/api/submit-form/`) — no env var needed for
# the URL.
#
# This used to be a Cloudflare Worker (a PUBLIC_WORKER_URL env var pointing
# at a separate *.workers.dev deploy) until September 2026, when that
# Cloudflare account was lost. See HANDOVER.md §7A and worker/README.md if
# you ever need the old version for reference.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY is server-only — it must NOT be prefixed PUBLIC_ (that would
# bundle it into client-shipped JS). For production, set it as a Vercel
# project Environment Variable (Production + Preview + Development), not
# here. Uncomment the line below only for local `npm run dev` testing, and
# never commit the real key.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_actual_key_here
#
# PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY below are already needed for
# the admin dashboard; this route reuses them for best-effort submission
# capture into the same tables the dashboard reads from.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — the admin dashboard (src/pages/admin/) and blog. Both values
# below are safe in the browser — Row Level Security is the real boundary,
# enforced in supabase/migrations/0004_rls.sql. The SERVICE-ROLE key is NOT
# here; it only ever lives in the create-worker Supabase Edge Function.
# See SUPABASE-SETUP.md for the full setup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
